WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.148
One Google connection brings in Search Console, Google Analytics, and your Business Profile, each linked to its store. Here’s how to set it up, and what you get.

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:21.089
In the Admin console, open Apps. Under Marketing and website, choose Google, sign in with the Google account that manages your website and profile, and approve.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:27.272
Then pick your Search Console property, and your Google Analytics property. Both are read-only.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:37.269
Under Business Profile, tick the locations to use, and choose which store each one belongs to. A location Google hasn’t verified yet can’t take posts.

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:41.509
Save, and it all shows up in Marketing, under SEO and website.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:50.393
At the top is Google Search: clicks, how often you were shown, click-through rate, and your average position, each against the period before.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:01:02.247
Almost on page one lists searches where you sit just off the first page. Click Content ideas, and AI suggests posts and pages that answer them, each built on a real search.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.777
Like one of them? Write this post sends it straight to Social, ready to finish and schedule.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:18.708
Shown often, rarely clicked finds pages that show up but don’t get picked. Better title has AI write a new title and description from that page’s own searches.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:27.132
Further down is your Business Profile, store by store: views on Search and Maps, calls, directions, and website clicks.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:38.959
The profile checklist shows what helps you show up in local searches, and what’s missing. Reviews shows your rating, and the ones still waiting for a reply, which you answer from the Social inbox.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:46.717
And from Analytics: where your website visits come from, and the visits each post and campaign sends you, through tagged links.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:56.532
Approved posts can go out to your Business Profile, too. Apart from those posts and review replies, Worklynq never changes your website or your profile.

